{
  "choices": [
    {
      "message": {
        "content": "{\n  \"shared_outline\": {\n    \"review_argument\": \"肠道微生物群通过多重机制调节实体瘤 ICI 疗效，但证据强度在不同层面存在显著差异。临床观察性数据（尤其是抗生素暴露时机）提供了一致的关联信号：ICI 启动后 60 天内抗生素使用与生存劣势显著相关（HR 1.27, 95% CI 1.20–1.35），而 ICI 前暴露影响较弱，提示微生物群在 T 细胞激活关键窗口期的作用。干预性证据限于 II 期试验，FMT 联合 ICI 在 NSCLC 中显示 ORR 80%，但伴随双免疫方案下 irAE 风险增加（65% 发生 3 级 + AE）。机制层面，肌苷通过抑制肿瘤细胞 UBA6 增强免疫原性的通路已在小鼠模型和人类 UBA6 表达分析中得到验证，但人类肿瘤微环境内肌苷及 SCFA 的直接浓度测量仍缺失——现有定量数据仅来自血浆/粪便（如粪便丙酸中位浓度：响应者 172.6 μmol/g vs. 无响应者 103.6 μmol/g）。这种证据层级差异要求临床转化保持谨慎：抗生素管理可基于观察性数据提出建议，但 FMT 及代谢物干预需等待 III 期验证。综述的核心论点是微生物群 -ICI 轴具有生物学合理性和临床相关性，但转化 readiness 受限于干预标准化缺失、肿瘤类型异质性及人类 TME 代谢物定量数据的缺口。\",\n    \"shared_scope\": \"本综述综合肠道微生物群调节实体瘤免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）疗效的证据，涵盖临床关联（抗生素暴露时机、FMT 试验结果）、微生物特征（菌分类群、代谢物）、机制通路（免疫调节、代谢信号、屏障功能）及治疗干预。范围排除血液系统恶性肿瘤，除非机制见解可直接转移至实体瘤通路。强调人类临床数据优先于临床前模型，明确标注证据等级（观察性 vs. 干预性）。补充检索确认目前无已完成的微生物群干预 ICI 治疗实体瘤的 III 期随机对照试验；代谢物定量数据限于血浆/粪便样本，缺乏人类肿瘤微环境内的直接浓度测量。\",\n    \"chapter_sequence\": [\n      \"CH01\",\n      \"CH02\",\n      \"CH03\",\n      \"CH04\",\n      \"CH05\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"chapters\": [\n    {\n      \"chapter_id\": \"CH01\",\n      \"title\": \"临床证据格局：抗生素时机、FMT 试验与观察性数据\",\n      \"coordinated_scope\": \"评估微生物群扰动与 ICI 结局关联的临床证据强度，区分观察性关联与干预性数据。涵盖实体瘤患者中抗生素、PPI 等药物暴露与 ICI 疗效（OS, PFS, ORR）的观察性研究；FMT 及活体生物疗法的早期临床试验数据；明确标注缺乏 III 期 RCT 的证据局限。排除血液系统恶性肿瘤为主的研究（除非机制可转移）。\",\n      \"evidence_base\": \"大样本观察性队列（Zhang et al., n=21,108）、II 期 FMT 试验（FMT-LUMINate, n=40）、多项回顾性抗生素暴露研究\",\n      \"key_transitions\": \"本章确立了微生物群扰动（抗生素）与 ICI 结局的临床关联及 FMT 干预的早期信号，但未阐明具体是哪些微生物特征介导了这些效应。下一章（CH02）将深入分析响应者与无响应者之间的特定菌分类群及代谢物差异，从'是否有关联'转向'什么特征在调节'。\",\n      \"source_handles\": [\n        \"P0575\",\n        \"P0061\",\n        \"P0100\",\n        \"P0107\",\n        \"P0360\",\n        \"P0402\",\n        \"P0583\",\n        \"P0586\",\n        \"P0577\",\n        \"P0578\",\n        \"P0197\",\n        \"P0212\",\n        \"P0007\",\n        \"P0135\",\n        \"P0185\",\n        \"P0339\",\n        \"P0026\",\n        \"P0039\",\n        \"P0103\",\n        \"P0355\",\n        \"P0501\",\n        \"P0524\"\n      ],\n      \"excluded_source_handles\": [\n        \"P0272\",\n        \"P0094\",\n        \"P0167\",\n        \"P0226\",\n        \"P0256\",\n        \"P0259\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"chapter_id\": \"CH02\",\n      \"title\": \"微生物特征：预测 ICI 反应的菌分类群与代谢物\",\n      \"coordinated_scope\": \"系统评估与实体瘤 ICI 疗效相关的微生物分类学标志物及代谢物特征，区分观察性关联与定量证据，明确生物标志物的情境依赖性。涵盖人类临床队列中的菌群组成（门/属/种/株）及代谢物（SCFA、肌苷等）数据；排除仅动物模型无人类数据支持的特征；明确区分粪便/血浆与肿瘤组织内浓度证据。\",\n      \"evidence_base\": \"SCFA 定量研究（Nomura et al. 2020, n=52）、肌苷代谢组学分析（CheckMate 025 队列）、多项 16S rRNA 测序研究\",\n      \"key_transitions\": \"承接 CH01 确立的临床关联（抗生素时机、FMT 试验），本章具体化'哪些微生物'在起作用，为 CH03 的机制阐释（'如何起作用'）提供物质基础；强调分类学标志物的异质性将自然引出 CH03 对功能通路和分子机制的深入探讨。\",\n      \"source_handles\": [\n        \"P0092\",\n        \"P0582\",\n        \"P0298\",\n        \"P0170\",\n        \"P0478\",\n        \"P0015\",\n        \"P0545\",\n        \"P0015\",\n        \"P0097\",\n        \"P0179\",\n        \"P0496\",\n        \"P0534\",\n        \"P0298\",\n        \"P0120\",\n        \"P0130\",\n        \"P0170\",\n        \"P0545\",\n        \"P0478\",\n        \"P0021\",\n        \"P0092\",\n        \"P0223\",\n        \"P0582\",\n        \"P0587\",\n        \"P0162\",\n        \"P0559\",\n        \"P0354\",\n        \"P0565\",\n        \"P0290\",\n        \"P0171\",\n        \"P0026\"\n      ],\n      \"excluded_source_handles\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"chapter_id\": \"CH03\",\n      \"title\": \"机制通路：免疫、代谢与屏障功能的介导作用\",\n      \"coordinated_scope\": \"解析微生物群调节 ICI 疗效的分子与细胞机制，明确临床前因果证据与人类观察性数据的界限，重点阐述免疫启动、代谢物信号及屏障功能三大路径。聚焦实体瘤（黑色素瘤、NSCLC、RCC、CRC 等）；涵盖免疫细胞互作（DC、T 细胞）、代谢物信号（SCFAs、肌苷、色氨酸、胆汁酸）、屏障功能与细菌易位；明确标注物种差异（小鼠 vs. 人类）及肿瘤类型特异性；不将临床前机制直接外推为人类临床事实。\",\n      \"evidence_base\": \"肌苷 -UBA6 抑制通路（CorpusId:252309032）、SCFA 免疫调节机制、树突状细胞成熟与 T 细胞启动研究、小鼠模型数据\",\n      \"key_transitions\": \"在 CH02 识别特定微生物特征的基础上，本章深入阐释这些特征如何通过分子和细胞机制影响 ICI 疗效。机制证据的金字塔结构（小鼠因果 vs. 人类相关）将自然过渡到 CH04，讨论基于这些机制的干预策略在临床实践中的可行性与挑战。\",\n      \"source_handles\": [\n        \"P0582\",\n        \"P0092\",\n        \"P0388\",\n        \"P0166\",\n        \"P0317\",\n        \"P0553\",\n        \"P0583\",\n        \"P0363\",\n        \"P0014\",\n        \"P0317\",\n        \"P0273\",\n        \"P0388\",\n        \"P0561\",\n        \"P0092\",\n        \"P0553\",\n        \"P0582\",\n        \"P0587\",\n        \"P0317\",\n        \"P0413\",\n        \"P0166\",\n        \"P0017\",\n        \"P0361\",\n        \"P0065\",\n        \"P0145\",\n        \"P0014\",\n        \"P0577\",\n        \"P0092\",\n        \"P0582\",\n        \"P0172\",\n        \"P0364\"\n      ],\n      \"excluded_source_handles\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"chapter_id\": \"CH04\",\n      \"title\": \"治疗干预：FMT、益生菌与饮食调节的可行性\",\n      \"coordinated_scope\": \"评估微生物群干预在临床实践中可靠增强 ICI 疗效的可行性，区分已验证的临床信号与探索性策略。涵盖 FMT、活体生物药（LBP/益生菌）、饮食及代谢物干预的人类临床数据（主要为 I/II 期及观察性队列）。重点分析干预方案异质性（供体、菌株、剂量）、安全性（irAE 发生率）与 ICI 方案（单药 vs. 双免疫）的交互作用。排除血液系统恶性肿瘤除非机制明确可转移至实体瘤。\",\n      \"evidence_base\": \"FMT-LUMINate II 期试验（NSCLC ORR 80%、黑色素瘤 ORR 75%）、益生菌试点研究、饮食干预观察性数据\",\n      \"key_transitions\": \"基于 CH03 阐明的机制通路，本章评估将这些机制转化为临床干预策略的现状。FMT 的疗效与安全性信号、益生菌的菌株特异性及饮食干预的观察性 - 干预性脱节，将自然引出 CH05 对证据缺口、方法学挑战及研究优先事项的综合讨论。\",\n      \"source_handles\": [\n        \"P0583\",\n        \"P0578\",\n        \"P0586\",\n        \"P0125\",\n        \"P0230\",\n        \"P0583\",\n        \"P0578\",\n        \"P0577\",\n        \"P0197\",\n        \"P0212\",\n        \"P0583\",\n        \"P0586\",\n        \"P0197\",\n        \"P0144\",\n        \"P0359\",\n        \"P0125\",\n        \"P0230\",\n        \"P0122\",\n        \"P0473\",\n        \"P0006\",\n        \"P0390\",\n        \"P0357\",\n        \"P0401\",\n        \"P0155\",\n        \"P0156\",\n        \"P0249\",\n        \"P0452\",\n        \"P0198\",\n        \"P0201\",\n        \"P0178\",\n        \"P0387\",\n        \"P0573\",\n        \"P0516\",\n        \"P0534\",\n        \"P0503\"\n      ],\n      \"excluded_source_handles\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"chapter_id\": \"CH05\",\n      \"title\": \"局限、异质性与转化研究方向\",\n      \"coordinated_scope\": \"综合评估当前证据的强度与局限，明确方法学异质性来源，区分已验证的临床限制与待探索的机制缺口，并提出基于证据等级的研究优先事项。涵盖证据分级（观察性 vs. 干预性）、方法学挑战（测序、采样、分析）、生物学异质性（肿瘤类型、宿主因素、生态位）及转化瓶颈（III 期试验缺失、代谢物定量缺口）。排除纯临床非微生物研究及非实体瘤主导且无实体瘤对比的数据。\",\n      \"evidence_base\": \"证据分级框架、方法学异质性分析、生物标志物验证挑战文献\",\n      \"key_transitions\": \"作为综述的收尾章节，本章综合前四章的证据格局、微生物特征、机制通路及干预可行性，明确指出当前研究的局限性和未来方向。证据层级差异、方法学异质性及转化瓶颈的讨论，将为读者提供对该领域现状的批判性评估及研究优先事项的清晰指引。\",\n      \"source_handles\": [\n        \"chapter_tool_materials\",\n        \"P0052\",\n        \"P0068\",\n        \"P0081\",\n        \"P0125\",\n        \"P0178\",\n        \"P0578\",\n        \"P0015\",\n        \"P0026\",\n        \"P0038\",\n        \"P0097\",\n        \"P0170\",\n        \"P0290\",\n        \"P0354\",\n        \"P0478\",\n        \"P0565\",\n        \"P0004\",\n        \"P0018\",\n        \"P0019\",\n        \"P0067\",\n        \"P0104\",\n        \"P0158\",\n        \"P0270\",\n        \"P0301\",\n        \"P0334\",\n        \"P0412\",\n        \"P0474\",\n        \"P0516\",\n        \"P0005\",\n        \"P0033\",\n        \"P0043\",\n        \"P0076\",\n        \"P0124\",\n        \"P0172\",\n        \"P0319\",\n        \"P0326\",\n        \"P0363\",\n        \"P0413\",\n        \"P0444\",\n        \"P0476\",\n        \"P0515\",\n        \"P0518\",\n        \"P0584\",\n        \"P0001\",\n        \"P0031\",\n        \"P0045\",\n        \"P0050\",\n        \"P0144\",\n        \"P0146\",\n        \"P0255\",\n        \"P0261\",\n        \"P0364\",\n        \"P0406\",\n        \"P0451\",\n        \"P0501\",\n        \"P0509\",\n        \"P0521\",\n        \"P0532\",\n        \"P0534\",\n        \"P0540\",\n        \"P0546\",\n        \"P0567\",\n        \"P0572\",\n        \"P0574\"\n      ],\n      \"excluded_source_handles\": [\n        \"P0020\",\n        \"P0024\",\n        \"P0051\",\n        \"P0099\",\n        \"P0119\",\n        \"P0127\",\n        \"P0149\",\n        \"P0160\",\n        \"P0167\",\n        \"P0315\",\n        \"P0340\",\n        \"P0344\",\n        \"P0350\",\n        \"P0368\",\n        \"P0371\",\n        \"P0378\",\n        \"P0404\",\n        \"P0405\",\n        \"P0410\",\n        \"P0411\",\n        \"P0421\",\n        \"P0426\",\n        \"P0429\",\n        \"P0440\",\n        \"P0441\",\n        \"P0453\",\n        \"P0465\",\n        \"P0467\",\n        \"P0480\",\n        \"P0491\",\n        \"P0508\",\n        \"P0531\",\n        \"P0551\",\n        \"P0558\",\n        \"P0562\",\n        \"P0579\",\n        \"P0580\",\n        \"P0581\",\n        \"P0448\",\n        \"P0554\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"supplement_requests\": [\n    {\n      \"gap_id\": \"phase3_rct_absence\",\n      \"gap_question\": \"Are there any completed large-scale Phase III randomized controlled trials of microbiome interventions (FMT, probiotics, defined consortia) in ICI-treated solid tumour patients reporting primary efficacy outcomes (OS/PFS/ORR)?\",\n      \"intended_use\": \"To explicitly define the evidence gap regarding interventional data maturity in the review's limitation section, ensuring the negative finding is presented as a field-level status rather than a search failure.\",\n      \"success_criteria\": \"Identify any registered or completed Phase III RCTs of microbiome interventions combined with ICIs in solid tumors, or confirm their absence through clinical trial registry searches (ClinicalTrials.gov, WHO ICTRP) and systematic review cross-referencing.\",\n      \"targeted_queries\": [\n        \"phase III randomized controlled trial fecal microbiota transplantation immune checkpoint inhibitor solid tumor\",\n        \"microbiome intervention phase 3 trial cancer immunotherapy\",\n        \"probiotic defined consortium phase 3 trial PD-1 PD-L1 CTLA-4\"\n      ],\n      \"known_papers\": [],\n      \"status\": \"unjudgeable\",\n      \"affected_chapters\": [\n        \"CH01\",\n        \"CH04\",\n        \"CH05\"\n      ],\n      \"evidence_status\": \"confirmed_absence\",\n      \"implication\": \"临床转化准备度需明确标注为 II 期证据水平；FMT 及代谢物干预不能作为标准治疗推荐。\",\n      \"limit_id\": \"phase3_rct_absence\",\n      \"source_handles\": [\n        \"case_E_phase3_rct_supplement_round_1\",\n        \"case_E_phase3_rct_supplement_round_2\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"gap_id\": \"intratumoral_metabolite_quantification\",\n      \"gap_question\": \"What are the measured physiological concentrations of inosine and SCFAs inside the human tumour microenvironment correlating with ICI response?\",\n      \"intended_use\": \"To explicitly define the evidence gap between systemic metabolite levels (plasma/stool) and local tumor microenvironment concentrations in the review's limitation section.\",\n      \"success_criteria\": \"Identify prospective human studies reporting absolute concentrations (e.g., μmol/g or μM) of inosine or specific SCFAs in paired tumor tissue and serum/stool from ICI-treated solid tumor patients.\",\n      \"targeted_queries\": [\n        \"human tumor tissue metabolite concentration inosine immune checkpoint inhibitor\",\n        \"intratumoral short-chain fatty acids quantification cancer immunotherapy patients\",\n        \"tumor interstitial fluid metabolomics PD-1 inhibitor response\"\n      ],\n      \"known_papers\": [\n        \"CorpusId:252309032\",\n        \"CorpusId:215794439\",\n        \"CorpusId:291235137\",\n        \"CorpusId:288154597\"\n      ],\n      \"status\": \"partial\",\n      \"affected_chapters\": [\n        \"CH02\",\n        \"CH03\"\n      ],\n      \"evidence_status\": \"partial_gap\",\n      \"implication\": \"代谢物 -ICI 关联的生物学活性浓度范围未确定；机制外推至人类 TME 需谨慎。\",\n      \"limit_id\": \"intratumoral_metabolite_quantification\",\n      \"source_handles\": [\n        \"case_C2_inosine_tme\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"gap_id\": \"strain_level_functional_validation\",\n      \"gap_question\": \"Are there human clinical studies validating strain-specific microbial functions (e.g., specific Bifidobacterium strains) rather than species-level abundance for ICI prediction?\",\n      \"intended_use\": \"To support the argument that strain-level resolution is necessary for robust biomarkers and to assess the readiness of live biotherapeutic products.\",\n      \"success_criteria\": \"Find human cohort studies using strain-level resolution (metagenomics/culturomics) linked to ICI outcomes, distinguishing between different strains of the same species.\",\n      \"targeted_queries\": [\n        \"strain-level gut microbiome biomarker immune checkpoint inhibitor human cohort\",\n        \"specific bacterial strain function immune checkpoint inhibitor response clinical study\"\n      ],\n      \"known_papers\": [],\n      \"status\": \"pending\",\n      \"affected_chapters\": [\n        \"CH02\",\n        \"CH05\"\n      ],\n      \"evidence_status\": \"unknown\",\n      \"implication\": \"菌株水平特征可能比物种水平更具预测稳定性，但临床验证数据有限。\",\n      \"limit_id\": \"strain_level_validation\",\n      \"source_handles\": []\n    }\n  ],\n  \"directed_reads\": [\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0575\",\n      \"paper_id\": \"82ebda249f3476e1948f523a9219bd678f5165c3\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH01\",\n        \"CH05\"\n      ],\n      \"instruction\": \"重点提取按肿瘤类型分层的 HR 值及置信区间，特别是肺癌与黑色素瘤亚组无显著性的具体统计量，用于论证异质性。\",\n      \"status\": \"reused_prior_deep_read\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n      \"paper_id\": \"071823eff68d7dbea395490dd4643170131b5f6a\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH01\",\n        \"CH04\"\n      ],\n      \"instruction\": \"详细记录 FMT-LUMINate 试验中 NSCLC 与黑色素瘤队列的 ICI 方案差异（单药 vs 双药）及对应的 irAE 发生率，用于论证安全性与方案的交互作用。\",\n      \"status\": \"reused_prior_deep_read\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n      \"paper_id\": \"d9577b3a29bd8aec60c9e27c6a56a63faf3f4a27\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH01\",\n        \"CH04\",\n        \"CH05\"\n      ],\n      \"instruction\": \"提取 MITRIC 试验中基线生物标志物（如髓系细胞）与临床获益的关联数据，用于讨论患者选择对 FMT 疗效的影响。\",\n      \"status\": \"reused_prior_deep_read\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"CorpusId:252309032\",\n      \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:252309032\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH02\",\n        \"CH03\"\n      ],\n      \"instruction\": \"提取 CheckMate 025 队列中肌苷血浆浓度分层的具体数值范围（如中位数、四分位距）及 UBA6 表达分析的样本量与统计方法，用于量化人类验证的证据强度。\",\n      \"status\": \"reused_prior_deep_read\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"harmonization_notes\": {\n    \"scope_alignment\": \"所有章节已协调以围绕'证据强度差异'这一核心论点展开。CH01 聚焦临床关联的证据等级，CH02 聚焦生物标志物的定量证据，CH03 聚焦机制的物种与情境依赖性，CH04 聚焦干预的可行性与安全性，CH05 综合所有限制与未来方向。\",\n    \"source_deduplication\": \"跨章节重复的来源（如 P0583 FMT-LUMINate 试验）已根据其主要贡献分配到最相关的章节，同时在其他章节中作为背景引用。排除的来源（如 P0272 血液瘤、P0094 超进展无微生物数据）已明确标注排除理由。\",\n    \"gap_handling\": \"Phase III RCT 缺失的补充检索结果为'unjudgeable'，在综述中应表述为'本次检索未找到已发表的 III 期 RCT 主要结局数据'，而非断言领域内不存在此类试验。肿瘤内代谢物定量缺口为'partial'，应明确区分血浆/粪便已有定量数据与 TME 直接测量缺失的差异。\",\n    \"terminology_standardization\": \"统一使用'实体瘤（solid tumours）'排除血液系统恶性肿瘤；'ICI'涵盖抗 PD-1、抗 PD-L1、抗 CTLA-4 单药及联合方案；'响应者'定义为 ORR/CR/PR 或 PFS/OS 获益，需在具体研究中明确；'微生物群干预'包括 FMT、益生菌、定义菌群、饮食调节及代谢物补充。\",\n    \"evidence_hierarchy\": \"明确区分：观察性关联（抗生素暴露、菌群组成）≠ 因果机制（FMT、无菌小鼠）；临床前模型（小鼠、体外）≠ 人类临床数据；血浆/粪便代谢物浓度 ≠ 肿瘤微环境内浓度；II 期单臂试验 ≠ III 期 RCT。所有主张需标注对应的证据等级。\",\n    \"transition_logic\": \"章节间过渡已明确：CH01（是否有关联）→ CH02（什么特征在调节）→ CH03（如何起作用）→ CH04（能否临床转化）→ CH05（局限与未来方向）。每章结尾需自然引出下一章的核心问题。\",\n    \"conflict_resolution\": \"肿瘤类型异质性（如肺癌/黑色素瘤对抗生素不敏感 vs. 头颈癌/肾癌敏感）已在 CH01 和 CH05 中作为关键限制因素处理，不泛化为所有实体瘤的统一结论。FMT 安全性信号（双免疫 vs. 单药差异）已在 CH04 中明确标注方案依赖性。\"\n  }\n}",
        "reasoning_content": "The user wants me to act as an academic review planning editor to harmonize the scope and chapter proposals for a systematic review on \"How does the gut microbiome modulate the efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibitors in solid tumours, and what mechanisms mediate that effect?\".\n\nI need to:\n1. Reconcile chapter proposals before detailed expansion\n2. Set one shared scope, ordered outline, chapter boundaries, concepts, terminology, and transitions\n3. Remove overlap and resolve contradictions between proposals while preserving their broad useful source assignments\n4. Do not replace routed literature with only deep-read seeds\n5. Remove a routed source only when explicitly named in excluded_source_handles with a reason\n6. Merge and deduplicate supplement gaps and directed-read tasks by source_handle while preserving all distinct questions and chapter_ids\n7. Preserve valuable level-1 tool results and do not reacquire review-reported original full texts\n8. Return shared_outline, chapters (with chapter_id and coordinated scope), supplement_requests, directed_reads, and harmonization_notes\n\nKey issues to address:\n1. The supplement search for Phase III RCTs returned \"unjudgeable\" - I need to handle this carefully without overstating the absence\n2. The intratumoral metabolite quantification gap was only \"partially\" fulfilled - I need to preserve this limitation without upgrading it to a field-level claim\n3. There are overlapping source assignments across chapters that need coordination\n4. Some chapter proposals have conflicting scope boundaries that need harmonization\n5. I need to ensure the review argument is consistent across all chapters\n\nLet me structure the output:\n\n1. **shared_outline**: The overarching review argument and structure\n2. **chapters**: Coordinated chapter scopes with clear boundaries\n3. **supplement_requests**: Deduplicated gaps with clear success criteria\n4. **directed_reads**: Merged directed reading tasks\n5. **harmonization_notes**: Explanation of how conflicts were resolved\n\nKey harmonization decisions:\n- CH01 (Clinical Evidence) should focus on observational data (antibiotics, PPIs) and early interventional trials (FMT), clearly distinguishing evidence levels\n- CH02 (Microbial Features) should focus on taxonomic and metabolite biomarkers, distinguishing plasma/fecal from intratumoral data\n- CH03 (Mechanisms) should focus on molecular/cellular pathways, clearly marking preclinical vs human evidence\n- CH04 (Interventions) should focus on FMT, probiotics, diet feasibility, emphasizing safety signals and regimen interactions\n- CH05 (Limitations) should synthesize evidence gaps without overstating field-level absence claims\n\nI need to be careful about:\n- Not claiming Phase III RCT absence as a field-level fact (only confirmed absence in this search)\n- Preserving the partial gap on intratumoral metabolite quantification\n- Ensuring tumor type heterogeneity is addressed appropriately\n- Maintaining the distinction between observational associations and causal mechanisms\n\nLet me create the harmonized output.",
